repository-code: https://github.com/tasicarl/binaryfog
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24294394
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  The supermassive black hole binary background as a nuisance parameter in
  pulsar timing array searches for new physics. binaryfog supplies the
  distribution of gravitational wave backgrounds a holodeck population model
  predicts, without calling holodeck, marginalises over that distribution inside
  the free-spectrum likelihood, and profiles over the six astrophysical
  parameters under their observational priors.
keywords:
  - pulsar timing arrays
  - gravitational waves
  - supermassive black hole binaries
  - early universe
